    "created_at": "2016-06-20T10:25:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-20T10:25:44Z",
    "body": "Yeah, I suppose if they passed in all the metadata that is now set directly as arguments that could work.\n\n(Apparently some implementations, e.g., Gecko, do actually create `Document` first and are able to do so because of the reflected-in-JavaScript rather than created-in-JavaScript business. There's agreement though that even though that's the case it shouldn't be that way in the standard.)\n",
